<meta type=article>
  <title | Layer 1>
  <author | The Enscribe Project>
</meta>

<config toc toc-location=right toc-depth=2 />

Layer 1 is enscribe's semantic-HTML substrate — a vocabulary of HTML elements for academic content
(sections, figures, citations, notes, math, theorems, tables, and more). Because it is plain HTML+CSS,
a Layer 1 document is portable and interoperable rather than a bespoke format, and it is the
**canonical, archival representation** of a document — the form used for long-term storage and
interchange (JATS export among them).

Layer 1 is what the shorthand register **expands to**. Authors rarely write it by hand — not because
they cannot, but because the <a href="enscribe-shorthand.html" | Enscribe Shorthand> register is the
ergonomic way to produce it. This page introduces the idea and shows a few constructs; the
comprehensive set lives in the <a href="layer1-catalog.html" | Layer 1 catalog>.

<# #sec:expands | Shorthand expands to Layer 1 #>

Each construct below is shown three ways: the shorthand you write, the Layer 1 markup it expands to,
and the rendered result. Every example is pulled live from the vocabulary source — the same source the
<a href="layer1-catalog.html" | Layer 1 catalog> is generated from — so it cannot drift from the engine.

The Layer 1 block shows the canonical markup as the vocabulary stores it; where an element produces a
large subtree — rendered math, say — the markup elides it with `…` so the structure stays legible.

<sub-section #featured-section | `<section>`>

**Shorthand**

<code>
<section | Introduction>
The paper begins here.
</code>

**Layer 1**

<code>
<section>
  <section-title>Introduction</section-title>
  <p>The paper begins here.</p>
</section>
</code>

**Rendered**

<frame -numbered>
<section | Introduction>
The paper begins here.
</frame>

<sub-section #featured-fig | `<fig>`>

**Shorthand**

<code>
<fig src=elephant.jpg | An adult African elephant.>
</code>

**Layer 1**

<code>
<figure>
  <img src="elephant.jpg" alt="An adult African elephant." />
  <figcaption>An adult African elephant.</figcaption>
</figure>
</code>

**Rendered**

<frame -numbered>
<fig -numbered src=elephant.jpg | An adult African elephant.>
</frame>

<sub-section #featured-note | `<note>`>

**Shorthand**

<code>
Some text<note | A substantive note about the text.>.
</code>

**Layer 1**

<code>
Some text<note id="note-1">A substantive note about the text.</note>.
</code>

**Rendered**

<frame -numbered>
Some text<note | A substantive note about the text.>.
</frame>

<sub-section #featured-inline-math | `<inline-math>`>

**Shorthand**

<code>
The identity <$ a^2 + b^2 = c^2 $> holds for right triangles.
</code>

**Layer 1**

<code>
<p>The identity <inline-math><span class="katex">…</span></inline-math> holds for right triangles.</p>
</code>

**Rendered**

<frame -numbered>
The identity <$ a^2 + b^2 = c^2 $> holds for right triangles.
</frame>

<sub-section #featured-math | `<math>`>

**Shorthand**

<code>
<math>
E = mc^2
</math>
</code>

**Layer 1**

<code>
<math>(KaTeX-rendered HTML)</math>
</code>

**Rendered**

<frame -numbered>
<math>
E = mc^2
</math>
</frame>

<sub-section #featured-table | `<table>`>

**Shorthand**

<code>
| Name | Price |
|------|-------|
| foo  | 1     |
| bar  | 2     |
</code>

**Layer 1**

<code>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Name</th><th>Price</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>foo</td><td>1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>bar</td><td>2</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</code>

**Rendered**

<frame -numbered>
| Name | Price |
|------|-------|
| foo  | 1     |
| bar  | 2     |
</frame>

<sub-section #featured-theorem | `<theorem>`>

**Shorthand**

<code>
<theorem | If $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$ then the triangle is right-angled.>
</code>

**Layer 1**

<code>
<theorem>If $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$ then the triangle is right-angled.</theorem>
</code>

**Rendered**

<frame -numbered>
<theorem -numbered | If $a^2 + b^2 = c^2$ then the triangle is right-angled.>
</frame>

<sub-section #featured-dl | `<dl>`>

**Shorthand**

<code>
<dl>
  <dt | enscribe>
  <dd | An academic publishing system built on HTML+CSS+JS.>
  <dt | Layer 1>
  <dd | The canonical semantic HTML vocabulary.>
  <dt | Layer 2>
  <dd | The shorthand authoring syntax that compiles to Layer 1.>
</dl>
</code>

**Layer 1**

<code>
<dl>
  <dt>enscribe</dt>
  <dd>An academic publishing system built on HTML+CSS+JS.</dd>
  <dt>Layer 1</dt>
  <dd>The canonical semantic HTML vocabulary.</dd>
  <dt>Layer 2</dt>
  <dd>The shorthand authoring syntax that compiles to Layer 1.</dd>
</dl>
</code>

**Rendered**

<frame -numbered>
<dl>
  <dt | enscribe>
  <dd | An academic publishing system built on HTML+CSS+JS.>
  <dt | Layer 1>
  <dd | The canonical semantic HTML vocabulary.>
  <dt | Layer 2>
  <dd | The shorthand authoring syntax that compiles to Layer 1.>
</dl>
</frame>


